` tag for `prisma` points to a release candidate, 8.0.0-rc.33, and there is no `@prisma/client` with that version. The CLI and client versions have to match, so I installed the current stable 7.10.1 for `prisma`, `@prisma/client` and `@prisma/adapter-pg`.\n\n**What I added:**\n- **`prisma/schema.prisma`:**\n  - `User` has a unique `email`, an optional `name` and its posts.\n  - `Post` has a `title`, optional `content`, `published` defaulting to false, and one required author.\n- **`prisma.config.ts`:** reads `DATABASE_URL` from `.env`. In Prisma 7 the connection settings live here, not in the schema.\n- **`prisma/migrations/…_init/`:** the migration that created the tables.\n- **`script.ts`:** creates a user with one published post and one draft, then prints all users with their posts.\n- **`package.json`:** the new dependencies, plus two shortcuts, `db:generate` and `db:migrate`.\n- **`.gitignore`:** now ignores the generated client in `src/generated/`.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- The script adds a timestamp to the email so it can run more than once without hitting the unique constraint. Each run adds another user.\n- The generated client isn't committed, so a fresh clone needs `npm install && npm run db:generate` before the script will run.\n- `.env` and `src/index.ts` are unchanged.\n\nANSWER.md has the full write-up with the commands and the script's output. I haven't committed anything.","ttft_ms":3342,"type":"result","duration_ms":118523,"uuid":"6dd5e5e1-3fe0-42e2-9bb8-da662c1000b8","ttft_stream_ms":2284,"time_to_request_ms":592,"first_content_frame_ms":2284,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":20,"outputTokens":4600,"cacheReadInputTokens":236181,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12087,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2360122,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":734,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":12087,"canonicalModel":"claude